</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 195)</h2>
<p><b>Shared reviews survive a dropped connection.</b> A sleeping laptop, a wifi blip or a tunnel no longer ends the session.</p>
<ul>
<li>The connection retries on its own for about ten minutes, and the status line says <b>Reconnecting…</b> rather than going quiet or declaring failure.</li>
<li>When it comes back you're <b>caught up to wherever the review has got to</b> — no need for the host to touch anything.</li>
<li>If it does give up, the message says so plainly and reopening the invite rejoins.</li>
<li>A host who loses the relay but still has people on the local network keeps sharing with them instead of dropping the review.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
